(4819607, 696917, 95109, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I like the natural framing created by the trees. My only criticism would be due to the patch of ground (grass?) in the lower right corner.</td>', 'Great shot. I like the natural framing created by the trees. My only criticism would be due to the patch of ground (grass?) in the lower right corner.', '2008-07-11 17:10:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819616, 695716, 95109, '<td valign="top">This is a very cool shot. I like all the repeating patterns from the physical structures chimneys, bricks, roof, etc as well as the coloring  combined with the overall low saturation and atypical aspect ratio.</td>', 'This is a very cool shot. I like all the repeating patterns from the physical structures chimneys, bricks, roof, etc as well as the coloring  combined with the overall low saturation and atypical aspect ratio.', '2008-07-11 17:20:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819636, 695397, 95109, '<td valign="top">I''m not a fan of borders in general but this is one of the rare shots I''ve seen were I think it works. Even so I think I would have preferred it in solid black (without the white lines).</td>', 'I''m not a fan of borders in general but this is one of the rare shots I''ve seen were I think it works. Even so I think I would have preferred it in solid black (without the white lines).', '2008-07-11 17:30:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819705, 697037, 95109, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition of this shot. An alternative title could have been "nonsyncope nonvertigo". This deceptively simple S curve photo with it''s combination of tilted orientation and the angular receding walkway almost makes me dizzy. I also like how as my eye follows the pathway it doesn''t just end but becomes increasingly obscured by the vegetation until it disappears.</td>', 'I really like the composition of this shot. An alternative title could have been "nonsyncope nonvertigo". This deceptively simple S curve photo with it''s combination of tilted orientation and the angular receding walkway almost makes me dizzy. I also like how as my eye follows the pathway it doesn''t just end but becomes increasingly obscured by the vegetation until it disappears.', '2008-07-11 18:30:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819744, 696829, 95109, '<td valign="top">I really liked the subject matter and the unique take on the urban landscape but didn''t care for the shot itself. Did you consider any alternate crops or angles? I think I get what you were going for, but with it titled "croweded" there is just too much negative space from the sky in my opinion. Perhaps a tighter, maybe square crop of just the right side of the image might archive the claustrophobic effect better?</td>', 'I really liked the subject matter and the unique take on the urban landscape but didn''t care for the shot itself. Did you consider any alternate crops or angles? I think I get what you were going for, but with it titled "croweded" there is just too much negative space from the sky in my opinion. Perhaps a tighter, maybe square crop of just the right side of the image might archive the claustrophobic effect better?', '2008-07-11 18:48:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819755, 695899, 95109, '<td valign="top">Great title and shot. Something about the cloudless sky combined with the "island" of shadow around the tree... it feels like it would be a welcome respite from the heat.</td>', 'Great title and shot. Something about the cloudless sky combined with the "island" of shadow around the tree... it feels like it would be a welcome respite from the heat.', '2008-07-11 18:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819762, 696919, 42013, '<td valign="top">Nobody does greens like Achoo. I like the landscape comp on this one. It gives a little more scale to the falls. David-- are you sure the Doc didn''t at least write the title? ;)</td>', 'Nobody does greens like Achoo. I like the landscape comp on this one. It gives a little more scale to the falls. David-- are you sure the Doc didn''t at least write the title? ;)', '2008-07-11 18:59:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819763, 696277, 42013, '<td valign="top">What a great feeling of depth and utter scale. 8</td>', 'What a great feeling of depth and utter scale. 8', '2008-07-11 19:00:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819765, 696568, 42013, '<td valign="top">Impressive falls. Good S-curve throughout the image. 8</td>', 'Impressive falls. Good S-curve throughout the image. 8', '2008-07-11 19:00:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819766, 695486, 42013, '<td valign="top">Peaceful, well done. 8</td>', 'Peaceful, well done. 8', '2008-07-11 19:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819767, 696440, 42013, '<td valign="top">This pic is so iconically rural that it hurts! Nice light and clouds. 8</td>', 'This pic is so iconically rural that it hurts! Nice light and clouds. 8', '2008-07-11 19:01:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819768, 695577, 42013, '<td valign="top">I like the simple light and colors.</td>', 'I like the simple light and colors.', '2008-07-11 19:01:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819771, 696410, 42013, '<td valign="top">Very urban/industrial. Nice mix of lighting.</td>', 'Very urban/industrial. Nice mix of lighting.', '2008-07-11 19:02:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819773, 696510, 42013, '<td valign="top">Subtle landscape, looks like a field in France.</td>', 'Subtle landscape, looks like a field in France.', '2008-07-11 19:02:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819774, 697090, 42013, '<td valign="top">Love the framing-- The only thing I don''t like(and still cant quite put my finger on it)is that the trees are very low contrast with just a touch of detail. I''d almost rather see them silhouetted, giving more tonal weight to the swirling water. As it is, their tones aren''t much different than the water, making the whole scene rather muted. Make sense? I''d like to see you rework this one with advanced editing as I believe it could be taken from very good to great! 8<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-16 19:25:25.</i></td>', 'Love the framing-- The only thing I don''t like(and still cant quite put my finger on it)is that the trees are very low contrast with just a touch of detail. I''d almost rather see them silhouetted, giving more tonal weight to the swirling water. As it is, their tones aren''t much different than the water, making the whole scene rather muted. Make sense? I''d like to see you rework this one with advanced editing as I believe it could be taken from very good to great! 8', '2008-07-11 19:02:53.000000', '2008-07-16 20:25:25.000000', 1),
(4819775, 696994, 42013, '<td valign="top">Strong shapes and diagonals formed with the rocks and the small path.</td>', 'Strong shapes and diagonals formed with the rocks and the small path.', '2008-07-11 19:03:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819776, 697083, 42013, '<td valign="top">Maybe this is Jason''s. Or maybe not?? Quality has its imitators! ;)</td>', 'Maybe this is Jason''s. Or maybe not?? Quality has its imitators! ;)', '2008-07-11 19:03:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819777, 696557, 42013, '<td valign="top">What a peaceful scene. Makes me want to read a good book--or take a nap.</td>', 'What a peaceful scene. Makes me want to read a good book--or take a nap.', '2008-07-11 19:03:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4819778, 696913, 42013, '<td valign="top">Impressive by its very size alone. Your photo does a great job of showing the falls size compared to the people.</td>', 'Impressive by its very size alone. Your photo does a great job of showing the falls size compared to the people.', '2008-07-11 19:03:35.000000', NULL, 1),
