(4821060, 697002, 42013, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. Nicely done in all ways. I''ll be interested to see its location.</td>', 'Very pretty. Nicely done in all ways. I''ll be interested to see its location.', '2008-07-12 17:04:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4821068, 697070, 9668, '<td valign="top">I wonder if you shot lower down to the water if you''d get a better reflection. Interesting shot. But doesn''t have much to draw my attention in.</td>', 'I wonder if you shot lower down to the water if you''d get a better reflection. Interesting shot. But doesn''t have much to draw my attention in.', '2008-07-12 17:12:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4821069, 695769, 9668, '<td valign="top">Freshet? Cool title. Freshet: "A sudden overflow of a stream resulting from a heavy rain or a thaw." This looks more like a normal stream to me, but maybe it''s a freshet as well. Nice use of low shutter speed. Compositionally, it seems a little cluttered - not that there are too many things in the frame, but not all the things in the frame are working together to make the composition pop.</td>', 'Freshet? Cool title. Freshet: "A sudden overflow of a stream resulting from a heavy rain or a thaw." This looks more like a normal stream to me, but maybe it''s a freshet as well. Nice use of low shutter speed. Compositionally, it seems a little cluttered - not that there are too many things in the frame, but not all the things in the frame are working together to make the composition pop.', '2008-07-12 17:15:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4821071, 695172, 9668, '<td valign="top">Alright, this one is like a breath of fresh air. I went ooh, nice lighting. wait, what is that in the tree, cool! Interesting composition choice. I would rather the kid looking into the frame so the eye isn''t drawn out of the frame, and the darkness of the tree also draws the eye right. But the luminescence of the leaves and the background is quite nice. I wonder if the kid was placed further out on the branch (like in the upper left R.o.Thirds). Great shot though.</td>', 'Alright, this one is like a breath of fresh air. I went ooh, nice lighting. wait, what is that in the tree, cool! Interesting composition choice. I would rather the kid looking into the frame so the eye isn''t drawn out of the frame, and the darkness of the tree also draws the eye right. But the luminescence of the leaves and the background is quite nice. I wonder if the kid was placed further out on the branch (like in the upper left R.o.Thirds). Great shot though.', '2008-07-12 17:19:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4821073, 695889, 9668, '<td valign="top">Cool lighting. The flatness of the tonal values in the background is odd. Like you''ve done something in post processing to pull out the shadows, but it''s killed the contrast. This seems like an image you took sortof randomly, and tried to fit into this challenge - especially with the title. This is a candid picture of a golfer, not a landscape.</td>', 'Cool lighting. The flatness of the tonal values in the background is odd. Like you''ve done something in post processing to pull out the shadows, but it''s killed the contrast. This seems like an image you took sortof randomly, and tried to fit into this challenge - especially with the title. This is a candid picture of a golfer, not a landscape.', '2008-07-12 17:21:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(4821076, 697025, 9668, '<td valign="top">alteredshots?  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=696183" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Graffiti-Sucks</a>. Like this shot a lot better than that one. Especially because this one doesn''t have those lighting effects. The use of infrared (or whatever) is awesome. Why do you think graffiti sucks?</td>', 'alteredshots?  Graffiti-Sucks. Like this shot a lot better than that one. Especially because this one doesn''t have those lighting effects. The use of infrared (or whatever) is awesome. Why do you think graffiti sucks?', '2008-07-12 17:24:33.000000', NULL, 1),
