(4824125, 694701, 45755, '<td valign="top">land·scape  noun, verb, -scaped, -scap·ing. <br/>1. a section or expanse of rural scenery, usually extensive, that can be seen from a single viewpoint.  <br/>2. a picture representing natural inland or coastal scenery.  <br/>3. Fine Arts. the category of aesthetic subject matter in which natural scenery is represented.  <br/>4. Obsolete. a panoramic view of scenery; vista.</td>', 'land·scape  noun, verb, -scaped, -scap·ing. 1. a section or expanse of rural scenery, usually extensive, that can be seen from a single viewpoint.  2. a picture representing natural inland or coastal scenery.  3. Fine Arts. the category of aesthetic subject matter in which natural scenery is represented.  4. Obsolete. a panoramic view of scenery; vista.', '2008-07-14 13:01:10.000000', NULL, 1),
