(4832174, 696240, 95638, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by beckydi:</b></div><hr/><i> The water seems like such an odd/contrasting color to the glacier - I''m interested to know where this was taken!  Neat picture! </i></td></tr></table> it''s taken in iceland north of Eyjafjallajökull (//flickr.com/photos/viktororn/2645620573/)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-18 07:04:35.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by beckydi: The water seems like such an odd/contrasting color to the glacier - I''m interested to know where this was taken!  Neat picture!  it''s taken in iceland north of Eyjafjallajökull (//flickr.com/photos/viktororn/2645620573/)', '2008-07-18 08:02:51.000000', '2008-07-18 08:04:35.000000', 0),
(4832218, 696049, 67152, '<td valign="top">Awesome warm and rich light here Judi - I am a big fan of this one and this spot - great work as usual.  <br/> <br/>I hope you don''t mind, but here are a couple things I noticed...<br/> <br/>I just wonder if a slightly different crop or a slightly different composition may have taken this up even a higher notch for the DPC crowd.  The placement of the shore seems very centered, almost as if it is two shots - one of the shore and one of the water.  It seems to me that it was hard to decide how to crop to get the feel of the actual spot and this is a compromise.   Second, the crop of the top of the tree in the center also makes it seem ever so slightly missing something.  <br/> <br/>One thing that I think really makes this shot work, besides the incredible capture of the ''light'', is the diagonal line created by the shore and continued into the water below the trees on the right.</td>', 'Awesome warm and rich light here Judi - I am a big fan of this one and this spot - great work as usual.   I hope you don''t mind, but here are a couple things I noticed... I just wonder if a slightly different crop or a slightly different composition may have taken this up even a higher notch for the DPC crowd.  The placement of the shore seems very centered, almost as if it is two shots - one of the shore and one of the water.  It seems to me that it was hard to decide how to crop to get the feel of the actual spot and this is a compromise.   Second, the crop of the top of the tree in the center also makes it seem ever so slightly missing something.   One thing that I think really makes this shot work, besides the incredible capture of the ''light'', is the diagonal line created by the shore and continued into the water below the trees on the right.', '2008-07-18 09:16:03.000000', NULL, 0),
